## What Revtek Is NOT

- A mass-market aftermarket parts seller.
- A discount-focused automotive business.
- A generic car accessories shop.
- A brand that relies on exaggerated claims or excessive hype.
- A brand that modifies vehicles simply for attention.
- A purely technical workshop with no design perspective.
- A purely aesthetic styling brand with no technical consideration.
- A business that prioritizes sales over the quality of the overall project.

Revtek should never try too hard to communicate that it is premium.
The quality of the products, projects, execution, and presentation
should communicate this naturally.

